In fact, in many cases an even better location for a stash is _just
off_ a branch level, on the less-visited side.  That way you get the
convenience of having a stash near a branch, while minimizing the time
spent on the stash level.  (Monsters can only disturb your stash while
you're on the same level as it is.)  Such locations include:

 * The level just above the branch to the Mines.
 * The bottom levels of Sokoban and Vlad's Tower.
 * The first Quest level.
 * Fort Ludios.

But you really shouldn't worry too much about picking the perfect
location for your stash, especially in the early game.  Just make your
stash somewhere near where you happen to be when you feel the need to
stash stuff.  You can always move and consolidate your stashes later.


