My main inventory, insofar as circumstances permit, tends to include
the following:

 * Worn amulets, rings and armor.
 * Wielded melee weapon (and secondary if twoweaponing).
 * Quivered stack of daggers,
   + or, if playing an archer type: stack of arrows and bow,
   + in early game: any throwables I can find and carry.
 * Possibly a light polearm (spetum, maybe ranseur or fauchard).
 * Lizard corpse.
 * Pet treat (tripe or meatball / apple or carrot).
 * Possibly a (cursed) scroll of teleport for emergencies.
 * Wand of fire or lightning; possibly other combat or escape wands.
 * Emergency rings, such as conflict, even when not worn.
 * Unicorn horn (preferably blessed).
 * Key (or lock pick or credit card if no keys).
 * Whistle (preferably magic).
 * Leash (especially if I have no magic whistle).
 * Mirror.
 * Pick-axe, *if* it won't make me burdened.
 * Bag.
 * Towel or blindfold.
 * Lamp or other light source, if expecting darkness.
 * Hard gem or ring (unless I happen to have an athame).
 * Luckstone (preferably blessed).

The bag, if I have one, should, if possible, contain:

 * Food, preferably lembas, pancakes or royal jelly.
 * Garlic, wolfsbane, maybe eucalyptus (especially if no unihorn).
 * Other potentially useful scrolls, potions, rings, wands, etc.
 * Some blank scrolls and a magic marker, if I have one.
 * A few valuable gems.
 * Blessed touchstone, if I have one and can afford the extra weight.

I like to carry a few emergency potions and scrolls, but they mostly
go into the bag as soon as I have one, since they're too easy to lose
if kept out in the open.  I may keep one scroll of teleport out in the
open for emergencies, though.  Potions are heavy, so I tend to carry
as few as possible, but one or two healing potions and/or a cursed
potion of gain level may literally save your life.  Taking a tinning
kit with me is always a temptation, but they weigh *a lot*.

This list doesn't include whatever stuff I may be trying to carry from
place A to place B at the moment, nor have I listed various useful but
rare items (like stethoscopes) that I'll carry if I happen to find one.

Note that this list mostly applies to the early- to midgame.  Later
on, as you acquire more magical items and face different dangers, the
priorities change somewhat.

The common theme with all these items is that either they allow me to
do something obviously useful that I couldn't do without them (hence
the large number of tools listed, and the even larger number of
unlisted tools that I'd carry if I had one) or they might save me from
some potentially lethal situation.  This is particularly important to
keep in mind: if you get in trouble and escape, you can go back to
your stash and pick up whatever you might need to properly deal with
it.  If you can't escape, you may very likely die.

Please note if you see anything clearly useful missing from the list;
I may have forgotten something.

